'"\\emph{valuative} if that order is total. \\emph{Infinitesimal}
homomorphisms, \\emph{birhizomicity at} a map, and \\emph{birhizomic covers}
are used exactly as in the problem statement. For a monoid "'$P$: $A_P$ is
the category of homomorphisms $P'"\\to Q"'$ of monoids; $B_P'"\\subseteq A_P"'$ is
the full subcategory of the objects $P'"\\to P[-c]"'^{'"\\sharp}"'$ ($c'"\\in P"'$);
$A_P''^{'"\\op}"'$ carries the birhizomic topology and $B_P''^{'"\\op}"'$ the trivial
topology; the inclusion $i:B_P''^{'"\\op}\\subset A_P"'^{'"\\op}"'$ induces
$'"\\pi"'^{-1}:'"\\Sh(B_P"'^{'"\\op})\\to\\Sh(A_P"'^{'"\\op})"'$ with right adjoint $'"\\pi_{*}"'$.

'"\\begin{theorem}\\label{thm:main}
For every monoid "'$P$ and every presheaf $F$ of abelian groups on
$B_P''^{'"\\op}"'$, the unit
'"\\[
\\eta_F:\\;F\\longrightarrow \\mathrm{R}\\pi_{*}\\pi"'^{-1}F
'"\\]
is a quasi-isomorphism; precisely, "'$F'"\\cong\\pi_{*}\\pi"'^{-1}F$ and
$'"\\mathrm{R}"'^{q}'"\\pi_{*}(\\pi"'^{-1}F)=0$ for all $q>0$.
'"\\end{theorem}

\\noindent\\textbf{Overview.}
\\S\\ref{sec:toolkit} (monoid toolkit): faces; rigidity of infinitesimal
maps (Lemma~\\ref{lem:inj}); discreteness of f.g.\\ ordered groups
(Lemma~\\ref{lem:discrete}); kernels in pushouts against valuative pieces
(Lemma~\\ref{lem:pushout}) with the \\emph{joint-span lemma}
(Lemma~\\ref{lem:jointspan}) and the \\emph{equiface theorem}
(Theorem~\\ref{thm:equiface}); the CFA and localization lemmas and the
\\emph{localization lemma} (Lemma~\\ref{lem:loc}), the one place where the
