\\emph{atlas construction} (Corollary~\\ref{cor:atlas-exists}): every
birhizomic cover refines to one made of tight \\emph{chart pieces}.
\\S\\ref{sec:sheaf}: "'$'"\\pi"'^{-1}F$ is the explicit presheaf $G_F=F'"\\circ B"'$
(Proposition~'"\\ref{prop:adj}); it is separated and satisfies descent
(Theorem~\\ref{thm:descent}) --- the proof works entirely in the filtered
colimit over covers, via a \\emph{comparison cover}
(Lemma~\\ref{lem:compare}) and separatedness; overlaps genuinely jump
