\\begin{proposition}[Faces]\\label{prop:faces}
Let "'$M$ be a monoid, $K'"\\subseteq M"'$ a face.
'"\\begin{enumerate}[label=\\textup{(\\alph*)},leftmargin=1.8em]
\\item "'$M/K:=(M'"\\setminus K)\\cup\\{0\\}"'$ '"\\textup{(}"'$0$ absorbing, addition
induced'"\\textup{)} is a monoid, "'$M'"\\to M/K"'$ is initial among homomorphisms
killing $K$, and $M/K'"\\cong M[-c]"'^{'"\\sharp}"'$ whenever $c$ generates the
face $K$.
'"\\item Faces are exactly the subsets "'$v''^{-1}(0)$ for $v:M'"\\to N"'$ with $N$
sharp; every face is finitely generated as a monoid; $M$ has finitely
many faces; $K'"\\mapsto(P\\to P/K)"'$ identifies $B_P$ with the poset of
faces of $P$ under inclusion: a morphism $(P'"\\to P/K_1)\\to(P\\to P/K_2)"'$
exists '"\\textup{(}uniquely\\textup{)} iff "'$K_1'"\\subseteq K_2"'$.
'"\\item "'$K''^{'"\\gp}\\cap P=K"'$; hence $K_1'"\\subseteq K_2\\iff
K_1"'^{'"\\gp}\\subseteq K_2"'^{'"\\gp}"'$; and the face generated by $K_1'"\\cup K_2"'$
has group $K_1''^{'"\\gp}+K_2"'^{'"\\gp}"'$.
