\\end{proposition}

\\begin{proof}
(a) If "'$x=k_1-k_2'"\\in M"'$ with $k_i'"\\in K"'$ then $x+k_2=k_1'"\\in K"'$, so
$x'"\\in K"'$; hence $M/K'"\\hookrightarrow M"'^{'"\\gp}/K"'^{'"\\gp}"'$. Sharpness of $M/K$
is the face property; saturation passes over; integrality is inherited;
initiality and the last clause are the universal properties of quotient,
localization, sharpening.
(b) $v(x)+v(y)=0$ in sharp $N$ gives $v(x)=v(y)=0$: $v''^{-1}(0)$ a face;
conversely $K='"\\ker(M\\to M/K)"'$. A face is a supporting-hyperplane section
of the f.g.'"\\ rational polyhedral "'$'"\\Cone(M)"'$: f.g.'"\\ (Gordan), finitely
many. Poset: as stated by initiality.
(c) The first claim is in (a); the group formula is immediate.
\\end{proof}

