submonoid "'$'"\\Sigma(v):=\\{x\\in P"'^{'"\\gp}:v"'^{'"\\gp}(x)\\in V\\}"'$, with lineality
$L_v='"\\ker(v"'^{'"\\gp})"'$; $'"\\Sigma(v)\\cap P=P"'$. Write
$'"\\bar P_v:=P/J_v\\hookrightarrow V"'$.
'"\\end{definition}

\\begin{lemma}[Discreteness]\\label{lem:discrete}
Let "'$'"\\Gamma"'$ be a finitely generated totally ordered abelian group,
convex chain
$0=H_0'"\\subsetneq H_1\\subsetneq\\cdots\\subsetneq H_s=\\Gamma"'$. Then each
$H_j/H_{j-1}$ has a least positive element and is $'"\\cong\\Z"'$. For chosen
positive lifts $'"\\gamma_j"'$, every $'"\\gamma=\\sum n_j\\gamma_j"'$ uniquely, and
$'"\\gamma>0"'$ iff its leading nonzero coefficient is positive.
'"\\end{lemma}

\\begin{proof}
An archimedean ordered group order-embeds in "'$('"\\R,+)"'$ (H'"\\\"older: fix
"'$a>0$; $g'"\\mapsto\\sup\\{m/n:mg\\le na\\}"'$). A f.g.'"\\ subgroup of "'$'"\\R"'$ is
discrete (its Euclidean minimum among generators generates), hence
infinite cyclic; archimedeanicity of $H_j/H_{j-1}$ is by definition of
the convex chain. Lift; the positivity criterion is immediate from
convexity (elements of $H_{j-1}$ are infinitesimal against $'"\\gamma_j"'$).
'"\\end{proof}

