\section{Statement}\label{sec:intro}

A \emph{monoid} is an integral, saturated, sharp, finitely generated
commutative monoid, written additively; it induces the translation
invariant partial order $x\ge0\iff x\in M$ on $M^{\gp}$ and is
\emph{valuative} if that order is total. \emph{Infinitesimal} maps,
\emph{birhizomicity at} a map, and \emph{birhizomic covers} are used
exactly as defined in the problem statement. For a monoid $P$: $A_P$ is
the category of monoid homomorphisms $P\to Q$; $B_P\subseteq A_P$ the
full subcategory of the objects $P\to P[-c]^{\sharp}$; $A_P^{\op}$
carries the birhizomic topology, $B_P^{\op}$ the trivial topology; the
inclusion $i:B_P^{\op}\subset A_P^{\op}$ induces
$\pi^{-1}:\Sh(B_P^{\op})\to\Sh(A_P^{\op})$ with right adjoint $\pi_{*}$.
We prove:

\begin{theorem}\label{thm:main}
For every monoid $P$ and every presheaf $F$ of abelian groups on
$B_P^{\op}$, the unit
\[
\eta_F:\ F\longrightarrow\mathrm{R}\pi_{*}\pi^{-1}F
\]
is a quasi-isomorphism; precisely, $F\cong\pi_{*}\pi^{-1}F$ and
$\mathrm{R}^{q}\pi_{*}(\pi^{-1}F)=0$ for all $q>0$.
\end{theorem}

